Reflection on the linear-memory ("low-level") wasm target, where TeaVM at 9be5eca57 left it as natives the backend
never implements (Class.getDeclaredFields/Methods/Constructors, annotations, type parameters, forName's name map,
Class.initialize, Array.get/set): the module links them as unresolved imports. That target never had reflection
metadata, so these now answer as a class with no reflectable members does: empty arrays, no annotations, no type
parameters; Class.forName throws ClassNotFoundException and forName(..., true, ...) initialises nothing. Array.get and
Array.set are implemented for real (Gson's ArrayTypeAdapter uses them).
Codegen: only on the low-level targets, and only in these methods.

